{"title":"Career roadmap — Talent Coordinator","role":"Talent Coordinator","summary":"A Talent Coordinator supports the identification, onboarding, scheduling, coordination and management of artists, performers, creators, actors, speakers, models, influencers or other talent for events, media productions, advertising campaigns and entertainment projects.","facts":{"Current degree":"BBA / BMS / BBM","Course":"BBA – Event / Media / Film Business"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role combines talent management + production coordination + communication + contracts + scheduling + client servicing. Strong professionals eventually move into talent management, casting, production, artist relations or entertainment business leadership."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build talent coordination, event/media production, communication, scheduling and contract-management skills; enter as Talent Coordinator/Artist Coordinator."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Progress to Talent Manager, Artist Manager, Casting Coordinator, Production Coordinator or Talent Acquisition Specialist."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move into Talent Manager, Casting Manager, Artist Relations Manager, Production Manager or Talent Partnerships roles."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead talent divisions, creator partnerships, casting operations or entertainment talent businesses; potentially become Head of Talent or Talent Agency Director."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Media + business foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Business communication"},{"text":"Event management"},{"text":"Media industry fundamentals"},{"text":"Film and entertainment business"},{"text":"Marketing"},{"text":"Consumer